---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-comment-thread</code> is a discussion for a record: a ticket, a document, an approval.
  It holds <code>wc-comment</code> elements, oldest first, and a composer under them. Replies are
  <code>wc-comment</code> elements with <code>slot="replies"</code> inside their comment; there is
  one level. The app owns the comments: every action fires an event and the app changes the
  elements.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 560px;'>
    <wc-comment-thread id='comment-thread-demo'>
      <wc-comment
        comment-id='1'
        author='Ada Lovelace'
        datetime='2026-11-06T09:30:00Z'
        href='#comment-1'
        body='Can we ship this on Friday?&#10;The release notes are ready.'
        editable
        deletable
      >
        <wc-comment
          slot='replies'
          comment-id='2'
          author='Grace Hopper'
          datetime='2026-11-06T10:02:00Z'
          body='Yes, the tests pass.'
          edited
        ></wc-comment>
      </wc-comment>
      <wc-comment comment-id='3' author='Alan Turing' datetime='2026-11-07T08:15:00Z' href='#comment-3'>
        <p style='margin: 0;'>Rich text goes in the comment: <b>bold</b>, <a href='#'>links</a>.</p>
      </wc-comment>
    </wc-comment-thread>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    const thread = document.querySelector('#comment-thread-demo');
    let nextId = 10;
    thread.addEventListener('submit', function (event) {
      const comment = document.createElement('wc-comment');
      comment.commentId = String(nextId++);
      comment.author = 'You';
      comment.datetime = new Date().toISOString();
      comment.body = event.detail.body;
      comment.editable = true;
      comment.deletable = true;
      if (event.detail.parentId) {
        comment.slot = 'replies';
        thread.querySelector('[comment-id="' + event.detail.parentId + '"]').append(comment);
      } else {
        thread.append(comment);
      }
      myConsole.log('submit: ' + JSON.stringify(event.detail));
    });
    thread.addEventListener('delete', function (event) {
      thread.querySelector('[comment-id="' + event.detail.commentId + '"]').remove();
      myConsole.log('delete: ' + event.detail.commentId);
    });
    thread.addEventListener('edit', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('edit: ' + event.detail.commentId);
    });
    thread.addEventListener('copy-link', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('copy-link: ' + event.detail.href);
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Composer</h3>
<p>
  <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> (<kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd>) or Send fires a cancelable
  <code>submit</code> with <code>detail.body</code> and <code>detail.parentId</code>
  (<code>null</code> for a new comment, the comment's <code>comment-id</code> for a reply). Unless
  the event is cancelled the composer empties and the app adds the comment. Put your own control in
  the <code>composer</code> slot (a mention input, say) to replace the textarea: it needs a
  <code>value</code> and must fire <code>input</code>.
</p>
